31. INFRASTRUCTURE PROVIDER INTERFACE

Prepare a provider-neutral TypeScript interface.

Do NOT call DigitalOcean.

Conceptually:

InfrastructureProvider

Future capabilities might include:

createCompute()
deleteCompute()
createNetwork()
createFirewall()
getResource()
getResourceStatus()

Do not overengineer this.

The goal is merely to prevent Phase 3 from embedding DigitalOcean API calls throughout unrelated business logic.

32. DEPLOYMENT PROVIDER INTERFACE

Similarly prepare a minimal boundary for a future deployment system.

Atlas may later use Coolify.

Conceptually:

DeploymentProvider

Possible future operations:

deployApplication()
getDeploymentStatus()
restartApplication()
deleteApplication()

Do NOT implement Coolify API calls.

